"""
patch_ask_ui_2026_10_22.py  ASK_UI_2026_10_22

Phase U1 (ask-ui) of docs/RELATIONS_AND_ASK_2026-10-22.md: one Ask page.

  scripts/ask.html      the page rewritten: the answer with numbered citations (a [tag] or [n] the model cites becomes
                        a number that opens its source; a tag not among the sources is shown dimmed); a little markdown
                        (paragraphs, lists, headings, bold); the sources beside the answer on a wide screen, below it on
                        a phone, each verse in Devanagari, IAST (on request) and English, the scholarly English first
                        where it passed, the working English (the one the answer read) behind it; badges for an e-text
                        witness, the scholarly English, the OCR engine, the text's state in the register, an editorial
                        item (which still opens its own page, BRAIN_ITEMS_2026_10_07); the names a verse names, each a
                        question to ask; "What this answer read", said plainly; copy with sources; recent questions and
                        the views remembered in this browser only; loading, error and spend-cap states; keyboard
                        (Ctrl+Enter, /) and phone.
  scripts/dashboard.py  _ask_enrich (new): /api/ask's sources also carry pid, sanskrit, iast, mt, ocr, witness, state,
                        scholar (with scholar_engine, scholar_state) and names, read from the same database, read-only
                        and free. The model is sent exactly what it was sent before: the answer does not change (that
                        is A1, ask-v2). A field it cannot read is left out; an error leaves the sources as they were.
  tests/test_ui_clarity_2026_10_22.py
                        its replay accepts a later patch's backup of dashboard.py (as test_docs76's does), since this
                        patch changes dashboard.py after UI_CLARITY.

The page is read from disk at each visit, so the new page shows at once; the sources' new fields come after the
dashboard is restarted (when it is idle). The old page works with the new dashboard and the new page with the old.

Needs BRAIN_ITEMS_2026_10_07 in dashboard.py and ask.html, UI_CLARITY_2026_10_22 in the test. Marker-idempotent per
file, all-or-nothing, backup first (.bak_askui_<date>), line endings kept, py_compile before anything is written.

  python scripts\\patch_ask_ui_2026_10_22.py --check
  python scripts\\patch_ask_ui_2026_10_22.py
"""
